# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this, `docker build ./portal` ships node_modules (hundreds of MB,
# and host-specific binaries) into the daemon, and .env files follow the
# repo to whatever registry builds the image. .dockerignore is the second
# line of defence after .gitignore for exactly that reason.

node_modules
.next
.git

# Never bake credentials into a layer. `make deploy` excludes .env from
# rsync too, but a local `docker build` has no such protection.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# Tests and type definitions are not runtime inputs.
tests
playwright-report
test-results
